IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 3, SUBPARTS 2 TO 4: EDITORIAL CHANGES, REVISION BILLS (ss 84 to 100).
-- ss 84, 92 and 93 (purpose and overview) create no rule: see the coverage table in NOTES.md. s 100 (what the PCO's annual report may address) is a permission with no limit and is encoded as one.
-- A person's interest here: what the PCO may change in a published version without changing the law, when a change takes effect, and what a revision Bill may and may not do.

§ `Section 85 -- Interpretation (editorial changes)`

-- src:628 | referential words means words that identify the whole or a part of a provision (including a schedule) as a provision, or as part of a provision, of the legislation in which they appear (for example, of this Act, of this section, of this paragraph, the said, and hereof).
-- "referential words means words that identify the whole or a part of a provision (including a schedule) as a provision, or as part of a provision, of the legislation in which they appear (for example, of this Act, of this section, of this paragraph, the said, and hereof)."
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 85, definition of referential words (src:628)
GIVEN `they identify the whole or a part of a provision as a provision, or as part of a provision, of the legislation in which they appear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are referential words` `they identify the whole or a part of a provision as a provision, or as part of a provision, of the legislation in which they appear` MEANS
    `they identify the whole or a part of a provision as a provision, or as part of a provision, of the legislation in which they appear`

-- src:627 | current drafting practice means the legislative drafting practice for the time being used by the PCO
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 85, definition of current drafting practice (src:627)
GIVEN `it is the legislative drafting practice for the time being used by the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is current drafting practice` `it is the legislative drafting practice for the time being used by the PCO` MEANS
    `it is the legislative drafting practice for the time being used by the PCO`

§ `Section 86 -- Power to make editorial changes`

-- Each printed item of section 87 is a member, and so is each thing it names (ruling C): the printed phrase comes first, its constituents follow.
DECLARE `Kind of editorial change` IS ONE OF
    `language indicating a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language`
    `language that indicates a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language`
    `language that could be taken to indicate a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language`
    `language to which section 16 applies changed to reflect section 16`
    `a reference to a changed name or title replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to a body whose name or title has changed replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to an office whose name or title has changed replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to a person whose name or title has changed replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to a place whose name or title has changed replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to a thing whose name or title has changed replaced with the name or title as changed`
    `a reference to a replaced body, office, person, place or thing changed to the replacement`
    `a reference to a body that has been replaced changed to the replacement body`
    `a reference to an office that has been replaced changed to the replacement office`
    `a reference to a person who has been replaced changed to the replacement person`
    `a reference to a place that has been replaced changed to the replacement place`
    `a reference to a thing that has been replaced changed to the replacement thing`
    `numbering, renumbering and consequential amendments authorised by an Order in Council under section 88`
    `numbering authorised by an Order in Council under section 88`
    `renumbering authorised by an Order in Council under section 88`
    `consequential amendments authorised by an Order in Council under section 88`
    `the way provisions are referred to changed to be consistent with current drafting practice`
    `unnecessary referential words omitted`
    `words in te reo Māori changed to reflect current orthographic conventions`
    `punctuation changed, omitted or inserted`
    `punctuation changed`
    `punctuation omitted`
    `punctuation inserted`
    `conjunctives and disjunctives inserted, omitted or changed`
    `conjunctives inserted, omitted or changed`
    `disjunctives inserted, omitted or changed`
    `the way numbers, dates, times, quantities, measurements and similar matters are expressed changed`
    `the way numbers are expressed changed`
    `the way dates are expressed changed`
    `the way times are expressed changed`
    `the way quantities are expressed changed`
    `the way measurements are expressed changed`
    `the way similar matters, ideas or concepts are expressed changed`
    `the way similar matters are expressed changed`
    `the way ideas are expressed changed`
    `the way concepts are expressed changed`
    `an obvious error corrected`
    `an obvious typographical or clerical error corrected`
    `an obvious typographical error corrected`
    `an obvious clerical error corrected`
    `an obvious grammatical or spelling error, or error of punctuation, corrected`
    `an obvious grammatical error corrected`
    `an obvious spelling error corrected`
    `an obvious error of punctuation corrected`
    `an obvious error in numbering, cross-referencing or alphabetical ordering corrected`
    `an obvious error in numbering corrected`
    `an obvious error in cross-referencing corrected`
    `an obvious error in alphabetical ordering corrected`
    `an obvious error in or arising out of an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected`
    `an obvious error in an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected`
    `an obvious error arising out of an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected`
    `any other obvious error of a similar nature corrected`
    `a method of setting or determining a date or time replaced with the exact date or time once set or determined`
    `a method of setting or determining a date replaced with the exact date once set or determined`
    `a method of setting or determining a time replaced with the exact time once set or determined`
    `a transitional, savings, validation or similar provision in amending legislation incorporated in the legislation it amends`
    `a transitional provision in amending legislation incorporated in the legislation it amends`
    `a savings provision in amending legislation incorporated in the legislation it amends`
    `a validation provision in amending legislation incorporated in the legislation it amends`
    `another similar provision in amending legislation incorporated in the legislation it amends`
    `changes made to show the effect of an amendment or repeal, or purely consequential on an amendment made by other legislation`
    `changes made to show the effect of an amendment`
    `changes made to show the effect of a repeal`
    `changes purely consequential on an amendment made by other legislation`
    `the Title of secondary legislation changed to better identify it or distinguish it from other legislation`
    `the Title of secondary legislation changed to better identify it`
    `the Title of secondary legislation changed to distinguish it from other legislation`
    `a change purely consequential on another change authorised by subpart 2`
    `a format change under section 89`
    `another change`

-- src:631 | Sections 87 and 89 do not permit any change to the text of a provision of any legislation that, if enacted, would change the effect of the provision.
-- src:632 | Nothing in this section limits the authority to make changes in reliance on the application of section 38 or any other legislation.
-- src:633 | 87 Editorial changes
-- src:634 | The following changes may be made under this subpart:
-- src:635 | language that indicates or could be taken to indicate a particular gender may be changed to gender-neutral language so that it is consistent with current drafting practice, as long as it is also consistent with the purpose of the legislation being changed:
-- src:636 | Examples
-- src:637 | The word he may be changed to they, or replaced with the relevant noun.
-- src:638 | The word chairman may be changed to chairperson.
-- src:639 | The words Her Majesty the Queen may be changed to the Sovereign.
-- src:640 | language to which section 16 applies may be changed to reflect the effect of section 16 (references to specific gender or kind of person include others):
-- src:641 | a reference to the name or title of a body, an office, a person, a place, or a thing that has been changed may be replaced with a reference to the name or title as changed:
-- src:642 | a reference to a body, an office, a person, a place, or a thing that has been replaced by another body, office, person, place, or thing may be changed to a reference to the replacement body, office, person, place, or thing:
-- src:643 | the numbering, renumbering, and consequential amendments authorised by an Order in Council made under section 88:
-- src:644 | changes may be made to the way provisions are referred to, so as to be consistent with current drafting practice:
-- src:645 | Example
-- src:646 | Schedule 1 to the Ombudsmen Act 1975 may be changed to Schedule 1 of the Ombudsmen Act 1975.
-- src:647 | unnecessary referential words may be omitted:
-- src:648 | changes may be made to words in the Māori language (te reo Māori) to reflect current orthographic conventions:
-- src:649 | punctuation may be changed or omitted, or new punctuation inserted, so as to be consistent with current drafting practice:
-- src:650 | conjunctives and disjunctives may be inserted, omitted, or changed so as to be consistent with current drafting practice:
-- src:651 | changes may be made to the way numbers, dates, times, quantities, measurements, and similar matters, ideas, or concepts are referred to or expressed so as to be consistent with current drafting practice:
-- src:652 | Example
-- src:653 | A reference in a form to this [blank] day of [blank] 19… may be changed to [Date].
-- src:654 | obvious errors of the following kinds may be corrected:
-- src:655 | typographical and clerical errors:
-- src:656 | grammatical and spelling errors, and errors of punctuation:
-- src:657 | errors in numbering, cross-referencing, and alphabetical ordering:
-- src:658 | errors in or arising out of an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed:
-- src:659 | any other errors of a similar nature:
-- src:660 | Examples
-- src:661 | In the following provision, the word in bold can be omitted: The board of a company may make offers on on one or more stock exchanges.
-- src:662 | An Act consequentially repeals section 85(3) of another Act. The other Act does not contain a section 85, and it is obvious from the context that the intention was to repeal section 75(3). The error can be corrected.
-- src:663 | An Act contains amendments to section 6 of another Act. Before the first Act comes into force, the other Act is amended so that section 6 is replaced by section 6A in substantially similar terms. Section 6A can be amended to reflect the intent of the amendments to section 6.
-- src:664 | a reference to a method of setting or determining a date or time (for example, a commencement that is calculated on a specified number of months after Royal assent) may be replaced with an exact reference to that date or time (once it is set or determined):
-- src:665 | Example
-- src:666 | A commencement clause states that the Act commences 6 months after Royal assent. If Royal assent is on 1 March 2020, this statement can be replaced with a statement that the Act commences on 1 September 2020.
-- src:667 | a provision in the nature of a transitional, savings, validation, or other similar provision that is contained in amending legislation may be incorporated as a provision of the legislation it amends, and all necessary consequential amendments may be made:
-- src:668 | changes may be made to show the effect of any amendment or repeal, and changes may be made that are purely consequential on any amendment made, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed:
-- src:669 | Example
-- src:670 | The heading to a section may be changed to reflect the effect of an amendment to the section.
-- src:671 | changes may be made to the Title of secondary legislation, so as to better identify the legislation or to distinguish it from other legislation:
-- src:672 | Examples
-- src:673 | The Cat Notice can be changed to the Cat Notice 2022, Cat Notice (No 5) 2022, or Cat Exemptions Notice 2022.
-- src:674 | The Exemptions Notice 2022, made under the Dogs and Cats Act 2020, can be changed to the Dogs and Cats (Exemptions) Notice 2022.
-- src:675 | changes may be made that are purely consequential on any other change authorised by this subpart.
-- Section 87 lists the changes; section 89 adds format changes; section 86(2) says neither permits a change to the text of a provision that, if enacted, would change its effect.
-- The "condition" input is the one condition the item itself attaches: consistent with the purpose of the legislation (gender-neutral language); the Order in Council exists (numbering); the error is obvious
-- (errors; for "any other errors of a similar nature" it means obvious and of a similar nature to the four before); the date or time has been set (exact dates); the legislation is secondary legislation (Title); the format is consistent with current drafting practice or easier to read or use (format). Items with no condition ignore it.
-- src:682 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make format changes to a version of legislation so that the format of the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice, or the format of the version of the legislation is easier to read or use according to the means used to read it, or both.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 86(2), s 87 and s 89 (src:631) (src:634-675) (src:682)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of editorial change`
      `the condition the item attaches is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would change the effect of the provision if enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a change of this kind may be made under subpart 2` kind `when its own condition is met:` `the condition the item attaches is met` `and it would change the effect of the provision if enacted:` `it would change the effect of the provision if enacted` MEANS
    IF `it would change the effect of the provision if enacted`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         -- The items that attach a condition (and, with it, "as long as" or "if"): the condition failing means subpart 2 does not give the change (JUST FALSE, ruling B).
         WHEN `language indicating a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `language that indicates a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `language that could be taken to indicate a particular gender changed to gender-neutral language` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `numbering, renumbering and consequential amendments authorised by an Order in Council under section 88` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `numbering authorised by an Order in Council under section 88` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `renumbering authorised by an Order in Council under section 88` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `consequential amendments authorised by an Order in Council under section 88` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious typographical or clerical error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious typographical error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious clerical error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious grammatical or spelling error, or error of punctuation, corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious grammatical error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious spelling error corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error of punctuation corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in numbering, cross-referencing or alphabetical ordering corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in numbering corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in cross-referencing corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in alphabetical ordering corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in or arising out of an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error in an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `an obvious error arising out of an amendment, by other legislation, to the legislation being changed corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `any other obvious error of a similar nature corrected` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `a method of setting or determining a date or time replaced with the exact date or time once set or determined` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `a method of setting or determining a date replaced with the exact date once set or determined` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `a method of setting or determining a time replaced with the exact time once set or determined` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `the Title of secondary legislation changed to better identify it or distinguish it from other legislation` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `the Title of secondary legislation changed to better identify it` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `the Title of secondary legislation changed to distinguish it from other legislation` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         WHEN `a format change under section 89` THEN JUST `the condition the item attaches is met`
         -- Section 87 says "The following changes may be made under this subpart", so a change that is not on the list is not given by subpart 2 (JUST FALSE); section 86(3) leaves other authority alone, which is the s 86(1) function's NOTHING.
         WHEN `another change` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make changes referred to in section 87 to a version of the legislation.
-- Section 86(3) says nothing in the section limits authority to make changes in reliance on section 38 or any other legislation, so without the Chief Parliamentary Counsel's authority under s 86(1) the section does not say the PCO may NOT make the change: NOTHING (ruling B keeps NOTHING here).
-- src:630 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make changes referred to in section 87 to a version of the legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 86(1) (src:630)
GIVEN `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has authorised the PCO to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
      permitted IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the PCO may make the change` `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has authorised the PCO to make it` `when subpart 2 permits it:` permitted MEANS
    IF `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has authorised the PCO to make it`
    THEN permitted
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) Nothing in section 86 limits the authority to make changes in reliance on the application of section 38 or any other legislation.
-- src:632 | Nothing in this section limits the authority to make changes in reliance on the application of section 38 or any other legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 86(3) (src:632)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 86 limits the authority to make changes in reliance on section 38 or any other legislation` MEANS FALSE

§ `Section 88 -- Changes to numbering`

-- src:677 | For the purpose of making legislation easier to find, use, or understand, the Governor-General may, by Order in Council, authorise the PCO to—
-- src:678 | publish a version of any specified legislation with provisions numbered or renumbered in the manner indicated by the order; and
-- src:679 | publish a version of any other specified legislation, in the manner indicated by the order, so as to consequentially update any references in that legislation to those numbered or renumbered provisions.
-- src:676 | 88 Changes to numbering
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 88(1) (src:676) (src:677-679)
GIVEN `it is made by Order in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is making legislation easier to find, use or understand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor-General may authorise the PCO to publish a renumbered or consequentially updated version` `it is made by Order in Council` `the purpose is making legislation easier to find, use or understand` MEANS
    `it is made by Order in Council` AND `the purpose is making legislation easier to find, use or understand`

-- src:680 | An order under this section is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 88(2) (src:680)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an order under section 88 is secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 89 -- Changes to format`

-- src:681 | 89 Changes to format
-- src:682 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make format changes to a version of legislation so that the format of the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice, or the format of the version of the legislation is easier to read or use according to the means used to read it, or both.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 89 (src:681) (src:682)
GIVEN `the format is made consistent with current drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the format is made easier to read or use according to the means used to read it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the format change is within section 89` `the format is made consistent with current drafting practice` `the format is made easier to read or use according to the means used to read it` MEANS
    `the format is made consistent with current drafting practice` OR `the format is made easier to read or use according to the means used to read it`

§ `Section 90 -- When changes take effect`

-- src:683 | 90 When changes take effect
-- src:684 | For the purposes of amendments to, incorporation of, or reference to legislation that has had changes made to it under this subpart, those changes take effect as if enacted or made expressly by other legislation having effect immediately before the date on which the changes were made.
-- For amendments to, incorporation of, or reference to legislation that has had changes made to it under this subpart, those changes take effect as if enacted or made expressly by other legislation having effect immediately before the date on which the
-- changes were made. So an amendment, incorporation or reference that takes effect on or after that date sees the changes; one that took effect before does not (fork F10 on the day itself).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 90 (src:683) (src:684)
GIVEN `the day the amendment, incorporation or reference takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day the changes were made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the changes are treated as already enacted for an amendment, incorporation or reference taking effect on` `the day the amendment, incorporation or reference takes effect` `to legislation changed on` `the day the changes were made` MEANS
    `the day the amendment, incorporation or reference takes effect` AT LEAST `the day the changes were made`

§ `Section 91 -- Changes to legislation to be noted on legislation website`

-- src:685 | 91 Changes to legislation to be noted on legislation website
-- src:686 | If changes authorised by this subpart are made, the PCO must—
-- src:687 | indicate that fact in a suitable place in the legislation or otherwise on the legislation website; and
-- src:688 | outline in general terms, and in a suitable place in the legislation or otherwise on the legislation website, the changes made.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 91 (src:685) (src:686-688)
GIVEN `changes authorised by subpart 2 have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must note the changes on the legislation website and outline them in general terms` `changes authorised by subpart 2 have been made` MEANS
    `changes authorised by subpart 2 have been made`

