    `it is a Bill prepared under subpart 3`

-- src:703 | revision programme means a revision programme approved under section 95.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 94, definition of revision programme (src:703)
GIVEN `it is a revision programme approved under section 95` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a revision programme` `it is a revision programme approved under section 95` MEANS
    `it is a revision programme approved under section 95`

§ `Section 95 -- Three-yearly revision programme`

DECLARE `Item a draft revision programme must set out` IS ONE OF
    `the revisions proposed to be started during the 3-year period`
    `the revisions expected to be enacted during that period`
    `the revisions on which work is expected to continue during that period`
    `anything else`

-- src:707 | A draft revision programme must set out—
-- src:708 | the revisions that are proposed to be started during the 3-year period; and
-- src:709 | the revisions that are expected to be enacted during that period; and
-- src:710 | the revisions on which work is expected to continue during that period.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): section 95(2) lists what the draft must set out, so what is off the list is not something this subsection requires: JUST FALSE.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 95(2) (src:707-710)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item a draft revision programme must set out`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a draft revision programme must set out` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `anything else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3) The Attorney-General must make the draft publicly available and invite submissions from interested persons and members of the public, allowing a reasonable time; and present a revision programme to the House as soon as practicable after it is approved by the Government.
-- src:711 | The Attorney-General must—
-- src:713 | present a revision programme to the House of Representatives as soon as practicable after it is approved by the Government.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 95(3) (src:711-713)
GIVEN `the draft was made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `submissions were invited, allowing a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a revision programme was presented to the House as soon as practicable after the Government approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3)` `the draft was made publicly available` `submissions were invited, allowing a reasonable time` `a revision programme was presented to the House as soon as practicable after the Government approved it` MEANS
    `the draft was made publicly available` AND `submissions were invited, allowing a reasonable time` AND `a revision programme was presented to the House as soon as practicable after the Government approved it`

-- (4) The Attorney-General may amend, or replace, the 3-yearly revision programme if the Attorney-General complies with subsection (3).
-- src:714 | The Attorney-General may amend, or replace, the 3-yearly revision programme if the Attorney-General complies with subsection (3) (applied as if the amendment or replacement were the draft or programme).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 95(4) (src:714)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3) as applied to the amendment or replacement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General may amend or replace the revision programme` `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3) as applied to the amendment or replacement` MEANS
    `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3) as applied to the amendment or replacement`

-- (1) The Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme for each new Parliament.
-- src:706 | The Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme for each new Parliament.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 95(1) (src:706)
GIVEN `it is for a new Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme` `it is for a new Parliament` MEANS
    `it is for a new Parliament`

§ `Section 96 -- Revision powers`

-- Each printed item of section 96(2) and (3) is a member, and so is each thing it names (ruling C): the printed phrase comes first, its constituents follow.
DECLARE `Change in a revision Bill` IS ONE OF
    `revising the whole or part of 1 or more Acts, combining or dividing Acts or parts of Acts`
    `revising the whole or part of 1 or more Acts`
    `combining Acts or parts of Acts`
    `dividing Acts or parts of Acts`
    `adopting a Title different from the Title or Titles of the Acts or parts revised`
    `omitting redundant and spent provisions`
    `omitting redundant provisions`
    `omitting spent provisions`
    `renumbering and rearranging provisions`
    `renumbering provisions`
    `rearranging provisions`
    `changes in language, format and punctuation for a clear, consistent, gender-neutral and modern style`
    `changes in language for a clear, consistent, gender-neutral and modern style`
    `changes in format for a clear, consistent, gender-neutral and modern style`
    `changes in punctuation for a clear, consistent, gender-neutral and modern style`
    `including new purpose, outline or overview provisions, examples, diagrams, graphics, flowcharts, readers' notes, lists of defined terms and similar devices`
    `including new or additional purpose provisions`
    `including new or additional outline provisions`
    `including new or additional overview provisions`
    `including new or additional examples`
    `including new or additional diagrams`
    `including new or additional graphics`
    `including new or additional flowcharts`
    `including new or additional readers' notes`
    `including new or additional lists of defined terms`
    `including other similar devices to aid accessibility and readability`
    `including new provisions alerting users to relevant legislation not incorporated in the revision`
    `correcting typographical, punctuation and grammatical errors and similar errors`
    `correcting typographical errors`
    `correcting punctuation errors`
    `correcting grammatical errors`
    `correcting other similar errors`
    `making consequential amendments to legislation not incorporated, or incorporated only in part, in the revision`
    `making consequential amendments to legislation not incorporated in the revision`
    `making consequential amendments to legislation incorporated only in part in the revision`
    `including necessary repeals, transitional, savings and related provisions`
    `including necessary repeals`
    `including necessary transitional provisions`
    `including necessary savings provisions`
    `including necessary related provisions`
    `making minor amendments to clarify Parliament's intent, resolve ambiguity or reconcile inconsistencies`
    `making minor amendments to reconcile inconsistencies`
    `making minor amendments to clarify Parliament's intent`
    `making minor amendments to resolve ambiguity`
    `making minor amendments to reconcile inconsistencies between provisions`
    `updating a monetary amount having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index, or providing for it to be prescribed by Order in Council`
    `updating a monetary amount having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index`
    `providing for a monetary amount to be prescribed by Order in Council`
    `making minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, or operate, to take account of changes in technology`
    `making minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, to take account of changes in technology`
    `making minor amendments to update how provisions operate, to take account of changes in technology`
    `omitting forms, schedules or other matters of detail and authorising them to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation`
    `omitting forms and authorising them to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation`
    `omitting schedules and authorising them to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation`
    `omitting other matters of detail and authorising them to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation`
    `including matters currently prescribed in secondary legislation made under the Acts or parts revised`
    `any other change necessary for implementing, or consequential on, the two changes above`
    `any other change necessary for implementing the two changes above`
    `any other change consequential on the two changes above`
    `a change that subpart 2 permits`
    `a change to the effect of the law not authorised by section 96(3)`
    `another change`

-- src:717 | A revision Bill may—
-- src:718 | revise the whole or part of 1 or more Acts, and for that purpose combine or divide Acts or parts of Acts:
-- src:719 | adopt a Title that is different from the Title or Titles of the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:720 | omit redundant and spent provisions:
-- src:721 | renumber and rearrange provisions from the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:722 | make changes in language, format, and punctuation to achieve a clear, consistent, gender-neutral, and modern style of expression, to achieve consistency with current drafting style and format, and generally to express better the spirit and meaning of the law:
-- src:723 | include new or additional purpose provisions, outline or overview provisions, examples, diagrams, graphics, flowcharts, readers’ notes, lists of defined terms, and other similar devices to aid accessibility and readability:
-- src:724 | include new or additional provisions alerting users of the revision to legislation that is not incorporated in the revision but is relevant to the subject matter of the revision:
-- src:725 | correct typographical, punctuation, and grammatical errors, and other similar errors:
-- src:726 | make consequential amendments to legislation that is not incorporated, or is incorporated only in part, in the revision:
-- src:727 | include any necessary repeals, transitional, savings, and related provisions.
-- src:728 | A revision Bill may also—
-- src:729 | make minor amendments to clarify Parliament’s intent, to resolve ambiguity, or to reconcile inconsistencies between provisions (or to do all of those things):
-- src:730 | update any monetary amount (other than an amount specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty), having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index over the relevant period, or provide for the amount to be prescribed by Order in Council:
-- src:731 | make minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, or operate, in a way that takes account of changes in technology if those amendments are consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law:
-- src:732 | for the purpose of enabling matters of general principle to be contained in Acts and matters of detail to be contained in secondary legislation,—
-- src:733 | omit forms, schedules, or other matters of detail from the Acts or parts of Acts revised, and instead authorise those matters to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation:
-- src:734 | include matters currently prescribed in secondary legislation made under the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:735 | make any other change that is necessary for the purpose of implementing subparagraph (i) or (ii) or that is consequential on doing so.
-- src:736 | In subsection (3)﻿(b), Consumers Price Index means the Consumers Price Index (all groups) published by Statistics New Zealand or, if that index ceases to be published, any measure certified by the Government Statistician as being equivalent to that index.
-- src:737 | A revision Bill must not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by subsection (3).
-- src:738 | The changes that may be made in a revision Bill include (without limitation) any of the changes that may be made under subpart 2.
-- (2) A revision Bill may do the things listed (a) to (j). (3) It may also make minor amendments to clarify intent; update any monetary amount (other than an amount specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty) having regard to the Consumers Price Index, or provide
-- for the amount to be prescribed by Order in Council; make minor amendments for changes in technology if consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law; move detail to secondary legislation and the reverse; and make other necessary or consequential changes.
-- (5) It must not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by (3). (6) The changes that may be made include (without limitation) any of the changes that may be made under subpart 2.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 96(2), (3), (5) and (6) (src:717-735) (src:737-738)
GIVEN change IS A `Change in a revision Bill`
      `the amount is specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology update is consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a revision Bill may make this change` change `when` `the amount is specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty` `and` `the technology update is consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `updating a monetary amount having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index, or providing for it to be prescribed by Order in Council` THEN JUST (NOT `the amount is specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty`)
    WHEN `updating a monetary amount having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index` THEN JUST (NOT `the amount is specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty`)
    WHEN `providing for a monetary amount to be prescribed by Order in Council` THEN JUST (NOT `the amount is specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty`)
    WHEN `making minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, or operate, to take account of changes in technology` THEN JUST `the technology update is consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law`
    WHEN `making minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, to take account of changes in technology` THEN JUST `the technology update is consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law`
    WHEN `making minor amendments to update how provisions operate, to take account of changes in technology` THEN JUST `the technology update is consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law`
    WHEN `a change to the effect of the law not authorised by section 96(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another change` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must prepare revision Bills in accordance with the current revision programme and this section.
-- src:716 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must prepare revision Bills in accordance with the current revision programme and this section.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 96(1) (src:716)
GIVEN `it is prepared in accordance with the current revision programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prepared in accordance with section 96` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has prepared the revision Bill as section 96(1) requires` `it is prepared in accordance with the current revision programme` `it is prepared in accordance with section 96` MEANS
    `it is prepared in accordance with the current revision programme` AND `it is prepared in accordance with section 96`

§ `Section 97 -- Format of revision Bill`

-- src:740 | A revision Bill must be in the form of a Bill suitable for introduction in the House of Representatives.
-- src:739 | 97 Format of revision Bill
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 97(1) (src:739) (src:740)
GIVEN `it is in the form of a Bill suitable for introduction in the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the revision Bill is in the required form` `it is in the form of a Bill suitable for introduction in the House of Representatives` MEANS
    `it is in the form of a Bill suitable for introduction in the House of Representatives`

-- src:741 | A revision Bill’s explanatory note must include a statement setting out, in general terms, the inconsistencies, anomalies, discrepancies, and omissions that were identified in the course of preparing the revision, and how they have been remedied in the Bill.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 97(2) (src:741)
GIVEN `the explanatory note states in general terms the inconsistencies, anomalies, discrepancies and omissions identified in preparing the revision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the explanatory note states how they have been remedied in the Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the explanatory note meets section 97(2)` `the explanatory note states in general terms the inconsistencies, anomalies, discrepancies and omissions identified in preparing the revision` `the explanatory note states how they have been remedied in the Bill` MEANS
    `the explanatory note states in general terms the inconsistencies, anomalies, discrepancies and omissions identified in preparing the revision` AND `the explanatory note states how they have been remedied in the Bill`

-- src:742 | A revision Bill may be structured so that it is able to be divided into 2 or more Bills.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 97(3) (src:742)
GIVEN `the Bill is structured so that it is able to be divided into 2 or more Bills` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a revision Bill may be structured to be divided into 2 or more Bills` `the Bill is structured so that it is able to be divided into 2 or more Bills` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 98 -- Certification of revision Bill`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `the President of the Law Commission`
    `the Solicitor-General`
    `a retired Judge of the High Court nominated by the Attorney-General`
    `a retired Judge of the High Court not nominated by the Attorney-General`
    `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`
    `anyone else`

-- src:744 | For the purposes of this subpart, the certifiers are the President of the Law Commission, the Solicitor-General, a retired Judge of the High Court nominated by the Attorney-General, and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
-- src:743 | 98 Certification of revision Bill
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 98(1) (src:743) (src:744)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a certifier` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `the President of the Law Commission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Solicitor-General` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a retired Judge of the High Court nominated by the Attorney-General` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a retired Judge of the High Court not nominated by the Attorney-General` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN FALSE

-- src:746 | The certifiers may certify a revision Bill if they are satisfied that—
-- src:748 | the revision Bill does not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by section 96(3).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 98(3) (src:746-748)
GIVEN `the revision powers in section 96 have been exercised appropriately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revision Bill does not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by section 96(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certifiers may certify the revision Bill` `the revision powers in section 96 have been exercised appropriately` `the revision Bill does not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by section 96(3)` MEANS
    `the revision powers in section 96 have been exercised appropriately` AND `the revision Bill does not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by section 96(3)`

-- src:745 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must submit a revision Bill to the certifiers for certification under this section.
-- src:749 | Before certifying a revision Bill, the certifiers may require the Chief Parliamentary Counsel to make whatever changes they consider necessary.
-- src:750 | When a revision Bill has been certified, the Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give the revision Bill and certificate to the Attorney-General.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 98(2), (4) and (5) (src:745) (src:749-750)
GIVEN `the revision Bill has been certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give the revision Bill and certificate to the Attorney-General` `the revision Bill has been certified` MEANS
    `the revision Bill has been certified`

§ `Section 99 -- Amendments proposed by revision Bills`

-- src:752 | A revision Bill, as introduced, must not contain any proposed change to the effect of the law unless the amendment is authorised by section 96.
-- src:751 | 99 Amendments proposed by revision Bills
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 99(1) (src:751) (src:752)
GIVEN `the proposed change is authorised by section 96` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a revision Bill as introduced may contain a proposed change to the effect of the law` `the proposed change is authorised by section 96` MEANS
    `the proposed change is authorised by section 96`

-- src:753 | However, nothing in this Act affects the powers of the House of Representatives to amend a revision Bill for any purpose and to pass it with amendment.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 99(2) (src:753)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act limits the powers of the House of Representatives to amend and pass a revision Bill` MEANS FALSE

§ `Section 100 -- PCO's annual report may address matters relating to revision and editorial changes`

DECLARE `Matter the PCO's annual report may address` IS ONE OF
    `a recommendation for the repeal of obsolete or redundant legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision`
    `a recommendation for the repeal of obsolete legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision`
    `a recommendation for the repeal of redundant legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision`
    `a recommendation for a change to the revision powers set out in section 96`
    `a recommendation for a change to the powers under subpart 2`
    `a recommendation for a change to the procedure for the certification of revision Bills`
    `any other matter`

-- src:754 | 100 PCO’s annual report may address matters relating to revision and editorial changes
-- src:755 | The PCO’s annual report under section 43 of the Public Finance Act 1989 may (without limitation) make—
-- src:756 | recommendations for the repeal of obsolete or redundant legislation or provisions of legislation, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision; and
-- src:757 | recommendations for changes to 1 or more of the following:
-- src:758 | the revision powers set out in section 96:
-- src:759 | the powers under subpart 2:
-- src:760 | the procedure for the certification of revision Bills.
-- The PCO's annual report under section 43 of the Public Finance Act 1989 may (without limitation) make the recommendations listed. "Without limitation" means a matter outside the list is not shut out either.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 100 (src:754) (src:755-760)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter the PCO's annual report may address`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO's annual report may make` matter MEANS TRUE
